# Kuberneted Namespaces 
- provides isoltaion to the resouces we create in kubernetes cluster
- what is resource ?
= Anything that we create in the kubernetes is called a resource ex: pod.
- every resource that we create under the kuberneted will go under the namespace.
- we can create/delete/get/descibe a resource in kubernetes, if we do not mention the namespace it will go under the "default" namespace.
- within a namespace we cannot have duplicate namespace.
- namespace allows you to restrict the access to the user who can access that.

# kubectl create namespace teama               -- create a new namespace teama
# kubectl create namespace teamb               -- create a new namespace teamb
# kubectl get namespace                        -- list of namespaces
